NODE id=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/ratelimit.Limiter.Purge kind=method
  digest=b3:255a31b58058420da42d119a34c40cd82037a966c3bb0111285035c925bb49d1 file=layerx/internal/ratelimit/ratelimit.go range=78:84 lang=go exported=true byte_range=2198:2599
  sig=func (l *Limiter) Purge(maxIdle time.Duration)
  doc=Purge drops buckets idle longer than maxIdle, bounding memory under a churn of\ndistinct keys. A key idle past maxIdle has, by construction, refilled to full\nburst (set maxIdle >> burst/rate), so dropping it is equivalent to resetting\nit to its default full-burst state — it never relaxes an active limit.
EDGES
  ^contains=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/ratelimit.Limiter
  ^defines=github.com/paxlabs-inc/layerx/internal/ratelimit/ratelimit.go

